/-!
# Inertia characterization and universal property of `G_{K,S}`

Let `K` be a number field and `S` a set of finite places of `K`. Let `K_S` be the maximal
subextension of `Kˢ / K` unramified at all finite places outside `S`, with Galois group
`G_{K,S} = Gal(K_S / K)` (`TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.galoisGroupS`).

This file connects `G_{K,S}` to local inertia subgroups at finite places outside `S`:

* For every finite place `v` of `K` and embedding `τ : Kˢ →ₐ[K] K_vˢ`, composing the local-to-global
  map `absoluteGaloisGroupMap τ : G_{K_v} →ₜ* G_K` with `restrictionS` gives
  `localToGaloisGroupS : G_{K_v} →ₜ* G_{K,S}`, which vanishes on local inertia whenever `v ∉ S`.
* Inside `G_K`, the closed subgroup `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S` generated by the images of local
  inertia subgroups at all `v ∉ S` (along all embeddings `τ : Kˢ →ₐ[K] K_vˢ`) equals the fixing
  subgroup of `K_S`, and hence equals `ker (restrictionS K (SeparableClosure K) S)`.
* Consequently, a continuous homomorphism `φ : G_K →ₜ* H` into a `T₁` topological monoid lifts
  uniquely to `liftGaloisGroupS : G_{K,S} →ₜ* H` whenever `φ` kills local inertia at all `v ∉ S`.

The final section gives the corresponding inclusion criteria in the algebraic-closure
model, using inertia subgroups at primes of the integral closure.

## Main definitions and results

* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.localToGaloisGroupS`: the continuous local-to-global map
  `G_{K_v} →ₜ* G_{K,S}`, with `localToGaloisGroupS_apply`,
  `galoisGroupSMap_comp_localToGaloisGroupS`, and `localToGaloisGroupS_eq_one_of_mem_inertia`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.inertiaOutsideSubgroup`: the closed normal subgroup of `G_K`
  generated by all local inertia subgroups at finite places outside `S`, with
  `inertiaOutsideSubgroup_def`, `inertiaOutsideSubgroup_le_iff_of_isClosed`, and
  `mem_inertiaOutsideSubgroup_iff`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.fixingSubgroup_maxUnramifiedOutside_eq_inertiaOutsideSubgroup`:
  the fixing subgroup of `K_S` equals `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.fixedField_inertiaOutsideSubgroup`: the fixed field of
  `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S` is `K_S`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.ker_restrictionS_eq_inertiaOutsideSubgroup`: the kernel
  of `G_K → G_{K,S}` is `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.liftGaloisGroupS` and
  `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.existsUnique_comp_restrictionS_eq`: universal property
  of `G_{K,S}` for continuous homomorphisms into `T₁` topological monoids.

* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.inertiaGroup_le_fixingSubgroup_maxUnramifiedOutside` and
  `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.fixingSubgroup_maxUnramifiedOutside_le`: the inclusion
  criteria in the algebraic-closure model.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Arithmetic Duality Theorems*, 2nd ed., Chapter I, §4.
* J. Neukirch, *Algebraic Number Theory*, Chapter II, §9.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

